    {
      "text": "Redevelops the Fish Market Restaurant site",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001041"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "July 2022 pre-application plan (SF YIMBY): 321 rental units (24 studios, 188 one-bedrooms, 109 two-bedrooms), five stories, 55 feet, 268,550 sq ft of housing, 376-car garage, 24 very low-income units, 3.18-acre site.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-002500"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Applicant notes from the June 22, 2022 neighborhood meeting say the Fish Market owners own the restaurant and the land, approached Windy Hill, and are partners in the development who may keep partial ownership.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-002502"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The City's February 21, 2024 incomplete letter lists the application as PA-2022-099, SUP + SPAR + SDPA, for APN 035-383-200, and asks that the project description reflect mixed use, three-bedroom units and a lot reconfiguration.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-002501"
      ]
